# AstraOS package archives (chroot stage).
#
# Format: "<deb-line> <pin-priority or empty>"
#
# The pinned *release* suite is deliberately not repeated here. live-build writes it from the
# mirror options in config/live-build/auto/config (--mirror-chroot and --archive-areas) and
# installs that file as /etc/apt/sources.list.d/zz-sources.list. Listing the same suite again
# here made every apt run inside the chroot report each target as "configured multiple times",
# which is noise a reviewer then has to explain away:
#
#   W: Target Packages (main/binary-amd64/Packages) is configured multiple times in
#      /etc/apt/sources.list.d/astraos.list:13 and /etc/apt/sources.list.d/zz-sources.list:1
#
# What live-build cannot add for this base release are the update and security suites: with
# --updates true / --security true it writes the pre-2017 "<suite>/updates" spelling, and
# Debian 13 has no such suite, so apt inside the chroot could not refresh it. Those two are
# therefore pinned by name here, and were verified against the real archive.
#
# Every entry is an authenticated Debian archive over the official mirror. AstraOS adds no
# third-party repository, PPA or unsigned source (plan §2.3, §13.3). debian-archive-keyring is
# part of the base system, so APT signature verification stays enabled, and the build also
# passes APT::Get::AllowUnauthenticated=false (see auto/config).

deb http://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-updates main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
deb http://security.debian.org/debian-security trixie-security main contrib non-free non-free-firmware

# NOTE: no backports. AstraOS 0.1.0 Alpha ships only packages from the pinned stable release
# plus its security and update suites, so a released image cannot silently pick up a newer ABI
# from an unrelated suite (plan §5).
